// Bindings for the deployed Cloudflare worker.
//
// Nitro reads this file at build time and merges it into the wrangler.json it
// writes to .output/server/, so this is the one place a service is attached to
// the worker. Nothing in it is needed to run the app locally.
//
// The worker has no writable disk, so with no binding an account only lives as
// long as the isolate that accepted it. This one is a D1 database: SQLite that
// belongs to the same Cloudflare account as the worker. The app keeps the whole
// document as a single JSON value in a single row — no schema beyond
// migrations/0001_document.sql, which it also creates on first use if allowed.
//
// To set up a new one:
//   1. npx wrangler d1 create muis   (prints a database_id)
//   2. put that id in database_id below
//   3. npx wrangler d1 execute MUIS_DB --remote --file=migrations/0001_document.sql
//   4. npx wrangler deploy
//
// `database_name` is left out on purpose: the binding is all a Worker needs, and
// naming the database again is a second thing to get wrong. The CLI targets it
// by the binding name instead — MUIS_DB above.
//
// Without the binding the worker answers exactly as it always has: it keeps
// accounts in memory, and everything that does not need an account keeps working.
{
  "d1_databases": [
    {
      "binding": "MUIS_DB",
      "database_id": "92829035-dfaa-4025-91fd-02f6c5e948dd"
    }
  ]
}
